To compile the mex file mkrak.c 

  (a) Check the Makefile and mexopts.sh for your own situation.
  (b) Execute make to make the object files.
      Also runs mex mkrak.c to make the mex file.
  (d) Run the test cases "runkrak1.m", "runkrak2.m", "runkrak3.m" in matlab 
      (and watch matlab crash...)

This code was developed using the free sunstudio f95 and C compilers
http://developers.sun.com/sunstudio/

The gnu gcc/gfortran compilers should also work, with some coaxing.  It is important 
to have fortran and c compilers that are compatible.  Matlab is very tempermental
about that.  See the mex directory for an example mexopts.sh file (mexopts.sh.gcc)

I've stored the necessary libraries for the sunstudio binary "mkrak.mexa64" to 
run in the libs directory.  Execute something like:
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:/home/dushaw/matlab.kraken/libs
to tell matlab where to find the libraries.
Check with "ldd mkrak.mexa64" to be sure the libraries are found.  (The matlab
libraries will be found once matlab is started.)


B.D.D. 3/2010, revised 5/2010

